1
00:05:08,571 --> 00:05:14,571
Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done.

2
00:10:17,142 --> 00:10:23,142
The Boondock Saints is a action, thriller, crime film directed by Troy Duffy.

3
00:15:25,714 --> 00:15:31,714
Tired of the crime overrunning the streets of Boston, Irish Catholic twin brothers Conner and Murphy are inspired
by their faith to cleanse their hometown of evil with their own brand of zealous vigilante justice.

4
00:20:34,285 --> 00:20:40,285
As they hunt down and kill one notorious gangster after another, they
become controversial folk heroes in the community.

5
00:25:42,857 --> 00:25:48,857
But Paul Smecker, an eccentric FBI agent, is fast
closing in on their blood-soaked trail.

6
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:57,428
Paul Smecker, played by Willem Dafoe.

7
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Conner MacManus, played by Sean Patrick Flanery.

8
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
Murphy MacManus, played by Norman Reedus.

9
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:23,142
Rocco, played by David Della Rocco.

10
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Il Duce, played by Billy Connolly.

11
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Detective Dolly, played by David Ferry.

12
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
The Boondock Saints II: All Saints Day is a 2009 vigilante action thriller film written and
directed by Troy Duffy, based on a story he co-wrote with his brother Taylor.

13
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
A sequel to The Boondock Saints (1999), the film stars Sean Patrick Flanery, Norman
Reedus, Clifton Collins Jr., Julie Benz, Peter Fonda, and Billy Connolly.

14
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Set eight years after the events of the first film, it follows Irish fraternal twin brothers Connor and Murphy MacManus
(Flanery and Reedus) living a quiet life in Ireland with their father Noah, formerly known as "Il Duce" (Connolly).

15
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
However, when an assassin frames the twins for the murder of a Catholic priest, they return to Boston and join forces with Mexican
underground fighter Romeo (Collins, Jr.) and FBI Special Agent Eunice Bloom (Benz), a former protégée of Paul Smecker.

16
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
The Boondock Saints II: All Saints Day had its world premiere in Boston on October 19,
2009, and was theatrically released in the United States on December 11, 2009.

17
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
Despite negative reviews from critics, the film was a modest success at the box
office, grossing $10.6 million against its $8 million budget.

18
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
A sequel is currently in development, with
Flanery and Reedus expected to return.

19
01:37:42,857 --> 01:37:48,857
The film explores themes of bratva (russian mafia), boston,
massachusetts, detective, irish-american, prologue.

20
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
